#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# lie_commutator_table

#% text
# `lie_commutator_table(gens, vars)` gives the matrix of the commutators `[v_i, v_j]` of the vector fields `gens` (lists of components over `vars`), each written as a combination of the basis elements `v(1)`, `v(2)`, ...

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The coordinates are found from the components at sample points (exact equations at rational points when the fields are rational, least squares at machine points otherwise) and checked symbolically. A commutator outside the span of `gens` is given by its components.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
lie_commutator_table([[2*x, y], [x^2, x*y], [1, 0]], [x, y])
#% output
#= [[0, 2*v(2), -2*v(3)], [-2*v(2), 0, -v(1)], [2*v(3), v(1), 0]]

#% text
# The symmetry algebra of the Korteweg-de Vries equation:

#% cell
lie_commutator_table(lie_point_symmetries(derivative(0, 1)(u)(x, t) + u(x, t)*derivative(1, 0)(u)(x, t) + derivative(3, 0)(u)(x, t) == 0, u, [x, t]), [x, t, u])
#% output
#= [[0, v(1), 0, v(3)], [-v(1), 0, (-1/3)*v(3), (2/3)*v(4)], [0, (1/3)*v(3), 0, 0], [-v(3), (-2/3)*v(4), 0, 0]]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `symmetry_commutator`, `lie_point_symmetries`
